e-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff112526/week-13-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Oklahoma State extends Morris with new 6-year deal","description":"Oklahoma State and head coach Eric Morris have agreed to a new six-year deal that will extend his contract through the 2032 season, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T17:00:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50594432/sources-oklahoma-state-extends-morris-new-six-year-deal","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Where is 'College GameDay'? 2026 schedule, locations, recaps","description":"What is the \"College GameDay\" schedule? Find out more about where the program will be each week of the 2026 college football season.","published":"2026-11-25T15:16:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49783645/where-college-gameday-2026-schedule-locations-recaps","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5150424/jordan-faison","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Faison"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jordan Faison","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Faison","description":"American football and lacrosse player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:20Z","intro":"Quincy Jordan Faison II (born April 7, 2004) is an American college football wide receiver for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish. He previously also played midfielder for the Notre Dame Fighting Irish lacrosse team.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Faison grew up in Weston, Florida and attended the Pine Crest School, where he played basketball, lacrosse, and football. In football, he played safety and quarterback in Pine Crest's Wing T offense and accumulated 1,800 all-purpose yards and scored 26 total touchdowns as a senior. Faison was a three-time All-American in lacrosse."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Faison entered his freshman football season at Notre Dame as a walk-on before earning a football scholarship midway through the season. He was named the MVP of the 2023 Sun Bowl after catching five passes for 115 yards and a touchdown in a 48–8 win over Oregon State. Faison finished his freshman football season with 19 receptions for 322 yards and four touchdowns.\nFaison was a starting midfielder in his freshman season with the Notre Dame Fighting Irish men's lacrosse team and scored 22 goals. He scored a goal in Notre Dame's 15–5 victory in the 2024 National Championship game against Maryland. He retired from lacrosse in January 2026 to focus fully on football."}]}}